WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.634 --> 00:00:03.570
-Michael, you are a great
comedian, and part of your job

00:00:03.570 --> 00:00:06.006
is to have strong opinions about
all different kinds of things.

00:00:06.006 --> 00:00:07.340
So with that in mind,
it's time to play

00:00:07.340 --> 00:00:09.776
a game we call
"Wheel of Opinions."

00:00:09.776 --> 00:00:10.843
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:10.843 --> 00:00:14.781
-♪ Wheel of opinions ♪

00:00:14.781 --> 00:00:16.549
-Now, here's how this works.
I'm going to hit this button,

00:00:16.549 --> 00:00:19.552
which activates the Opinion
Topic Generator, okay?

00:00:19.552 --> 00:00:21.154
It will land on a random topic.

00:00:21.154 --> 00:00:23.023
Whatever it is, you have
to give your opinion on it.

00:00:23.023 --> 00:00:25.959
-I'm with it.
-Alright, here we go.

00:00:25.959 --> 00:00:27.726 line:0%
[ Beeping ]

00:00:27.726 --> 00:00:31.130 line:0%
-What was that?

00:00:31.130 --> 00:00:32.431 line:0%
-The phrase --
-Oh.

00:00:32.431 --> 00:00:33.799 line:0%
-The phrase "let's do lunch."

00:00:33.799 --> 00:00:36.235 line:0%
-I hate that phrase,
"let's do lunch,"

00:00:36.235 --> 00:00:39.606 line:0%
because it's usually followed by
"just so I can pick your brain."

00:00:39.606 --> 00:00:41.807 line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:41.807 --> 00:00:44.711 line:0%
I hate that idea that people
think if they buy me --

00:00:44.711 --> 00:00:46.912 line:0%
What is lunch,
like a sandwich and a salad?

00:00:46.912 --> 00:00:48.982 line:0%
And you want --
You want me to tell you

00:00:48.982 --> 00:00:51.217 line:0%
everything that I know
about show business?

00:00:51.217 --> 00:00:52.952 line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:52.952 --> 00:00:54.287 line:0%
For a sandwich?

00:00:54.287 --> 00:00:55.454 line:0%
-Pick your brain.

00:00:55.454 --> 00:00:57.056 line:0%
-I hate pick your brain.

00:00:57.056 --> 00:00:58.158 line:0%
No. Ugh.

00:00:58.158 --> 00:00:59.659 line:0%
Pass.

00:00:59.659 --> 00:01:00.960 line:0%
-Let's do lunch.

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:02.228 line:0%
-I hate that.

00:01:02.228 --> 00:01:03.796 line:0%
[ Beeping ]

00:01:03.796 --> 00:01:05.464 line:0%
-I see popcorn in there,
cruise ships.

00:01:05.464 --> 00:01:07.834 line:0%
-What's this? Oh.
-Pink lemonade.

00:01:07.834 --> 00:01:09.702 line:0%
-I don't know --

00:01:09.702 --> 00:01:10.803 line:0%
Okay.

00:01:10.803 --> 00:01:12.438 line:0%
I know what pink lemonade is,

00:01:12.438 --> 00:01:15.308 line:0%
but I don't --
I don't know what the pink is.

00:01:15.308 --> 00:01:17.776 line:0%
-No, me, neither.
-Because lemonade is just lemon.

00:01:17.776 --> 00:01:19.145 line:0%
-Yes.
-And pink lemonade

00:01:19.145 --> 00:01:21.180 line:0%
tastes different
than regular lemonade.

00:01:21.180 --> 00:01:22.549 line:0%
-It does.
-But then what is the pink?

00:01:22.549 --> 00:01:23.582 line:0%
'Cause it's not strawberry,

00:01:23.582 --> 00:01:25.518 line:0%
'cause that's
strawberry lemonade.

00:01:25.518 --> 00:01:27.687 line:0%
So then what is the pink
in the pink lemonade?

00:01:27.687 --> 00:01:28.988 line:0%
-What is pink lemonade?

00:01:28.988 --> 00:01:32.058 line:0%
It does have a bit
of a more flavorful lemonade.

00:01:32.058 --> 00:01:34.794 line:0%
-Yeah, it tastes pink,
but I don't know --

00:01:34.794 --> 00:01:37.030 line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:37.030 --> 00:01:38.364 line:0%
I don't know what pink is --

00:01:38.364 --> 00:01:41.568 line:0%
For some reason, pink, purple,
and red has a flavor,

00:01:41.568 --> 00:01:43.736 line:0%
and we don't know
where those come from.

00:01:43.736 --> 00:01:45.504 line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:45.504 --> 00:01:47.573 line:0%
-Let's get another topic.
Here we go.

00:01:47.573 --> 00:01:50.876 line:0%
[ Beeping ]
-These are random as hell.

00:01:50.876 --> 00:01:52.211 line:0%
-They're all --

00:01:52.211 --> 00:01:53.813 line:0%
[ Sputters ]

00:01:53.813 --> 00:01:55.247 line:0%
Bees. What's your opinion --

00:01:55.247 --> 00:01:56.415 line:0%
Do you have an opinion on bees?

00:01:56.415 --> 00:01:59.752 line:0%
-I -- Uh, yeah. Kind of. Sure.

00:01:59.752 --> 00:02:01.187 line:0%
For the sake of this game.

00:02:01.187 --> 00:02:02.555 line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:02.555 --> 00:02:04.623 line:0%
I don't -- Okay,
here's the thing about bees.

00:02:04.623 --> 00:02:07.827 line:0%
Like, the world's going to end
because the bees are gone,

00:02:07.827 --> 00:02:10.262 line:0%
and nobody predicted that.

00:02:10.262 --> 00:02:13.432 line:0%
Why wouldn't that be
one of the commandments?

00:02:13.432 --> 00:02:16.335 line:0%
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:16.335 --> 00:02:17.669 line:0%
Why wouldn't they tell us?

00:02:17.669 --> 00:02:19.338 line:0%
Like, "Oh, by the way,

00:02:19.338 --> 00:02:21.641 line:0%
keep the bees alive,
or it's over."

00:02:21.641 --> 00:02:23.609 line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:23.609 --> 00:02:25.411 line:0%
-Yeah, that's interesting.
Like, Nostradamus --

00:02:25.411 --> 00:02:27.713 line:0%
No one predicted it.
-No one said the bees.

00:02:27.713 --> 00:02:30.950 line:0%
We just found out that
we just got to keep the bees.

00:02:30.950 --> 00:02:32.352 line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:32.352 --> 00:02:33.753 line:0%
I like to think
when God comes back,

00:02:33.753 --> 00:02:37.123 line:0%
he's going to be like,
"Where are all the bees?"

00:02:37.123 --> 00:02:38.691 line:0%
I left billions."

00:02:38.691 --> 00:02:41.427 line:0%
-"Yeah, I invented this amazing
thing."

00:02:41.427 --> 00:02:43.195 line:0%
-It's all bees.
The world's going to end

00:02:43.195 --> 00:02:44.330 line:0%
because of the bees.

00:02:44.330 --> 00:02:46.398 line:0%
-That's such a great
opinion on bees.

00:02:46.398 --> 00:02:48.600 line:0%
I had no idea you were
going to go there. Wow.

00:02:48.600 --> 00:02:50.870 line:0%
[ Cheers and applause ]
I thought you were gonna go,

00:02:50.870 --> 00:02:52.572 line:0%
"I like them. I hate them.
They sting."

00:02:52.572 --> 00:02:55.441 line:0%
-I got strong opinions about
stuff that no one cares about.

00:02:55.441 --> 00:02:57.977 line:0%
-[ Laughs ]
Let's try more. Why not?

00:02:57.977 --> 00:03:01.213 line:0%
[ Beeping ]

00:03:01.213 --> 00:03:03.849 line:0%
People who end e-mails
with, oh, "thoughts"?

00:03:03.849 --> 00:03:05.384 line:0%
That's not fair.
That's coming from --

00:03:05.384 --> 00:03:06.952 line:0%
'Cause I do that, dude.
-Do you really?

00:03:06.952 --> 00:03:08.721 line:0%
-Yeah.
-Oh, that sucks.

00:03:08.721 --> 00:03:10.290 line:0%
[ Laughter ]
-Come on, dude.

00:03:10.290 --> 00:03:11.724 line:0%
-That's like
the second-worst thing.

00:03:11.724 --> 00:03:14.860 line:0%
You know what I also hate
that's in the same vein?

00:03:14.860 --> 00:03:16.729 line:0%
I hate when people say,
"alright?"

00:03:16.729 --> 00:03:18.797 line:0%
on an answering machine.

00:03:18.797 --> 00:03:22.368 line:0%
Like, I can't tell you it's
alright! Like, it's just --

00:03:22.368 --> 00:03:24.737 line:0%
"Alright, I'll talk to you
later, alright? Alright, bye."

00:03:24.737 --> 00:03:27.406 line:0%
I hate that.
-Yeah, you're not talking back.

00:03:27.406 --> 00:03:29.509 line:0%
-Yeah. "Thoughts" is --
I don't -- You know, e-mails,

00:03:29.509 --> 00:03:32.044 line:0%
it's like, "I don't want
to give you my thoughts."

00:03:32.044 --> 00:03:33.846 line:0%
That's the whole reason
for an e-mail.

00:03:33.846 --> 00:03:35.915 line:0%
It's like informal so you don't
know what I'm thinking.

00:03:35.915 --> 00:03:38.618 line:0%
I'm just going to give you
whatever the three responses are

00:03:38.618 --> 00:03:41.053 line:0%
at the bottom of Gmail.

00:03:41.053 --> 00:03:42.588 line:0%
I'm just going to give you
one of those.

00:03:42.588 --> 00:03:45.158 line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:45.158 --> 00:03:46.425 line:0%
-Let's do one more, please.

00:03:46.425 --> 00:03:48.528 line:0%
Your final topic is --

00:03:48.528 --> 00:03:51.164 line:0%
[ Beeping ]

00:03:53.132 --> 00:03:55.068 line:0%
[ Audience groans, laughs ]

00:03:55.068 --> 00:03:56.469 line:0%
-Did one of those say toe rings?

00:03:56.469 --> 00:03:57.870 line:0%
-Yeah, I saw that, too.
Yeah, yeah.

00:03:57.870 --> 00:03:59.071 line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:59.071 --> 00:04:00.806 line:0%
What's your opinion, quickly,
on toe rings?

00:04:00.806 --> 00:04:02.742 line:0%
-Oh, I don't -- [ Laughs ]

00:04:02.742 --> 00:04:06.378 line:0%
I wear shoes, so --
I'm wearing 10 right now, but --

00:04:06.378 --> 00:04:07.947 line:0%
-One on each toe, man?
-Yeah, man.

00:04:07.947 --> 00:04:10.583 line:0%
I don't want kids.
I want adults.

00:04:10.583 --> 00:04:13.253 line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:14.120 --> 00:04:15.421 line:0%
I want adults. I don't want --

00:04:15.421 --> 00:04:17.890 line:0%
I have no interest
in the kid part of your life.

00:04:17.890 --> 00:04:20.460 line:0%
I don't know when people
got so obsessed with kids.

00:04:20.460 --> 00:04:23.529 line:0%
I have friends who have kids.
They were weird.

00:04:23.529 --> 00:04:25.164 line:0%
[ Laughter ]
And you go into their house,

00:04:25.164 --> 00:04:27.800 line:0%
and there's, like, toys in
the couch, and it drives me --

00:04:27.800 --> 00:04:30.269 line:0%
Since when are kids allowed
in the living room?

00:04:30.269 --> 00:04:32.571 line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:32.571 --> 00:04:33.740 line:0%
When did that start

00:04:33.740 --> 00:04:35.140 line:0%
that you could be in the --
-They run it.

00:04:35.140 --> 00:04:37.042 line:0%
-Yeah, they're like, "Oh,
do you want to play with Dylan?"

00:04:37.042 --> 00:04:38.511 line:0%
No, I'm a drunk man.

00:04:38.511 --> 00:04:41.313 line:0%
Why would I want
to play with Dylan?

00:04:41.313 --> 00:04:42.781 line:0%
-Michael Che, everybody.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:42.781 --> 00:04:45.818 line:0%
All episodes of
"That Damn Michael Che"

00:04:45.818 --> 00:04:48.588 line:0%
are streaming May 6th
on HBO Max.

